President Trump said nothing yesterday  about George Floyd's funeral but he did  take the time to spread a right-wing  conspiracy theory on Twitter about a 75  year old protester who was shoved to the  ground by Buffalo police and severely  injured the president's claims have no  known basis in fact Ben Tracy reports  from the White House the video was  shocking 75 year old Martin Gugino  shoved to the ground by police in  Buffalo New York last week blood poured  out of his ear as officers walked by on  Tuesday with no evidence President Trump  said Gugino could be an NT foe  provocateur who was trying to scan  police communications to black out the  equipment and that falling to the ground  could be a setup it's common antifa  tactics that a president was spreading a  conspiracy theory started by far-right  media sources Gugino a well-known local  peace activist is still in the hospital  in a statement his attorney said we are  at a loss to understand why the  President of the United States would  make such dark dangerous in untrue  accusations against him what do you  think it was it was staged do you think  the blood coming out of his head was  staged is that what you're saying you  saw his head hit the pavement you see  blood on the pavement New York Governor  Andrew Cuomo demanded president Trump  apologize  I don't think Donald Trump's going to  change his behavior several Republicans  tried to avoid the topic including the  president's own chief of staff Marc  meadows  Meadows visited Capitol Hill on Tuesday  to discuss police reforms with  Republican senator Tim Scott a draft  report of Scott's plan obtained by CBS  News includes new reporting requirements  for deadly use of force incidents by  police increase funding for body cameras  and de-escalation training so far the  White House has not said what if any  rope reforms it would support meanwhile  President Trump is still considering  giving a national address about race and  unity but the White House is trying to  figure out where to do that we are told  it is unlikely to be an oval office  address Gale all right Ben thank you  very much we'd all be listening
 

